 patches</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>114</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>445</fpage><lpage>457</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10469734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mageretal1993"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mager</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Naeve</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Quick</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Labarca</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lester</surname><given-names>H.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Steady states, charge movements, and rates for a cloned GABA transporter expressed in <italic>Xenopus</italic> oocytes</article-title><source>Neuron</source><volume>10</volume><year>1993</year><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7679914</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Mennericketal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mennerick</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shen</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Benz</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimamoto</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Isenberg</surname><given-names>K.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>J.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zorumski</surname><given-names>C.F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Substrate turnover by transporters curtails synaptic glutamate transients</article-title><source>J. Neurosci</source><volume>19</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>9242</fpage><lpage>9251</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10531428</pub-id></citati